# --- Project artefacts (regenerated, never tracked) ---
# Root-anchored: a bare `data/` would also match src/bkrobust/data/.
/results/*
!/results/.gitkeep
!/results/README.md
# The breakdown-radius demonstration's outputs ARE deliverables: report.md
# cites them and they are small CSV/JSON. Everything else under results/ is
# regenerated experiment output and stays untracked.
!/results/breakdown_radius_demo/
# Axis A / Axis B session outputs are deliverables too: the pre-registration,
# per-instance rows and manifests are cited by report_synth_and_search.md.
!/results/synth/
!/results/search/
# Session 2 (Axis B deep) outputs are deliverables cited by
# report_axisb_deep.md and THEOREMS.md.
!/results/axisb2/
!/results/axisb3/
!/results/axisb4/
!/results/axisa2/
!/results/axisa3/
# Axis Robustness (survival curves + Pareto frontier) outputs are deliverables
# cited by report_fragility_and_pareto.md; the pre-registration lives here too.
!/results/axis_robustness/
# Stage 0 of the evaluation plan: the claim-unit radius audit of the committed
# axisa3 rows, cited by docs/EVALUATION_PLAN.md and docs/PAPER_NARRATIVE.md.
!/results/stage0/
# Session 8 (the epsilon-bias radius) outputs are deliverables: every number in
# report_r_epsilon.md, docs/PAPER_INTEGRATION_R_EPSILON.md and
# paper/sections/epsilon-radius.tex traces to a file here, and the
# counterexample witnesses carry the SEMs needed to replay them. 936 KB total.
!/results/epsilon/
# The LLM background-knowledge elicitation (ported from ze/experiments): the
# frozen frame, questionnaire, per-condition answers and the knowledge sets K
# that the final table is computed at. The answer cache under
# results/elicit/cache/ stays untracked -- it regenerates in seconds from the
# committed remote answers via elicit_import.py.
!/results/frame/
!/results/elicit/
/results/elicit/cache/
# The final table: r_val and r_eps for every real network at its LLM-elicited
# K, per-instance rows plus the aggregate cited in the paper's results table.
!/results/final_table/
# The epsilon > 1 re-run of the final table (docs/RESULT_EPSILON_ABOVE_ONE.md):
# same schema as final_table, plus the per-instance staircase beta_up(d) and
# ceiling B(Chat) that make any future epsilon a lookup rather than a re-run.
!/results/final_table_eps_gt1/
# The exhaustive mean-vs-max shell study (docs/EXPERIMENT_MEAN_VS_MAX.md):
# every retraction state of 15 instances, with the full distribution of B per
# shell. Evidence for the shell-aggregation design decision.
!/results/mean_vs_max/
# The soundness gate for that design decision (docs/RESULT_MEAN_SOUNDNESS_GATE.md):
# the whole enumerated space per instance, with max and mean compared over the
# full sphere, the full ball and the retraction shell.
!/results/mean_fullspace/
# The mean bias profile mu(d) and everything that supports reporting it
# (docs/MEAN_REPORTING.md): the per-query table over the real corpus, the
# epsilon-grid selection, the bounding-statistic study, and the monotonicity
# search. results/mean_sampling/ is NOT tracked: its per-repetition draws run to
# 65 MB and every number cited is in its summary files, which are.
!/results/mean_table/
!/results/mean_epsilon/
!/results/mean_bounds/
!/results/mean_monotonicity/
!/results/mean_adaptive/
# The reporting table on the paper's own geometry (docs/MEAN_TABLE_FULLSPACE.md):
# mu over the full space G_Chat with BFS distance, per query, exhaustive.
!/results/mean_table_fullspace/
!/results/mean_sampling/
/results/mean_sampling/radius_reps.jsonl
/results/mean_sampling/shell_reps.jsonl
/results/mean_sampling/profile_audit.jsonl
# [RE-11]: survival and the paired cross-arm on the 831 real rows. The
# pre-registration, the frozen frame, the per-grid-point curve rows and the
# manifests are deliverables cited by report_real_survival.md and
# table_tau_real.md.
!/results/axis_robustness_real/
# The elicited-knowledge survival panel: the same survival/ranking design run
# with K read from results/elicit/knowledge.json instead of built by
# benchmarks.measure.select_knowledge, swept over all ten elicitation
# conditions. One shard per (condition, network). The per-grid-point curve
# rows, the per-instance rows and the manifest are the deliverables -- every
# reported number derives from them, and they are far smaller than the real
# arm's because there is no coverage x base-wrongness x replicate cross.
!/results/axis_robustness_llm/
# The repo-wide `*.log` rule (added for LaTeX) also catches this sweep's logs.
# The 240 per-shard logs are regenerable and their durable content -- elapsed
# time, cache hit counts, status counts, both file digests, the git sha and the
# knowledge.json digest -- is already in _done/<shard>.json. The panel-level log
# is the session's own timeline, so that one is kept.
!/results/axis_robustness_llm/_logs/panel_*.log
# Reviewer point 6: the N=1000 synthetic survival rerun (40 instances/cell, the
# originally pre-registered quota) carrying the corruption denominators and the
# new baseline predictors. The per-grid-point curves and the per-instance rows
# are the deliverables -- every reported number derives from them. The raw
# per-draw samples run to several GB and regenerate exactly from the seeded
# driver, so they stay untracked (precedent: results/mean_sampling/*_reps.jsonl).
!/results/axis_robustness_p6/
/results/axis_robustness_p6/shards/*/survival_samples.csv
/results/axis_robustness_p6/survival_samples.csv
/results/axis_robustness_p6/survival_samples.csv.gz
# Reviewer point 7: the three-way classification of every non-informative row in
# the final table (valid-empty vs no-set-exists vs invalid-returned).
!/results/zero_radius/
# Reviewer point 7: the matched-control elicitation arms -- scrambled-name
# semantic controls and the random-at-matched-|K| quantity control.
!/results/matched_control/
/results/matched_control/_shim/
# Reviewer point 6: the new baselines and the paired network-level resampling on
# the committed 831 real rows.
!/results/axis_robustness_real_p6/
# Reviewer point 6: the paired resampling applied to the synthetic N=1000 rerun.
!/results/axis_robustness_p6_paired/
/data/
